  "loc": "Abstract; Section 3",
  "quote": "we define the degree to which a given rule satisfies an axiom",
  "note": "The paper is a general framework for measuring probabilistic degrees of axiom satisfaction and for evaluating rules, with a Shapley-value-based compatibility measure. It is not about a voting procedure aggregating agents' inputs. Instances are abstract, and the examples come from fair division and general social choice."
